{"step_index":1608,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:58:34Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:58:34+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:58:34+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n<truncated 3 lines>\n{\"step_index\":1592,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:58:22Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:58:22+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:58:22+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nTesting if W=4 can ever have radius >= 4...\\r\\nPROVED: when W=4, radius <= 3 ALWAYS!\\r\\n\\n\"}\r\n{\"step_index\":1593,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:58:22Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Evaluating radius bound constraints**\\n\\nIf the width, *W*, is 4, then radius is at most 3, always. If *W* is 5 or greater and the radius is less than or equal to 4, then the radius + 1 is at most 5, which is less than or equal to *W*. This holds true in both cases of *W* = 4 and when *W* is >= 5.\\n\\nTherefore, for all graphs where the radius is less than or equal to 4, radius + 1 will always be less than or equal to *W*. The analysis now focuses on graphs with radius <= 5.\\n\\n\\n**Refining radius and width bounds**\\n\\nFor any *k*, if *W* <= 2*k*, the radius cannot be >= 2*k* because the maximum radius is bounded by floor(3W/4), which is less than W. The goal now is to prove this using theorem proving.  The existing approach, relying on a `sorry`, needs to be refined. The challenge is in proving the case where the radius is greater than 3.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_card_bound.lean\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"View test_card_bound.lean\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View test_card_bound.lean\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1594,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:58:27Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:58:27+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:58:27+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promisin\n<truncated 3061 bytes>\nmpr ⟨h_sub, h_not_eq.symm⟩\\n62:   exact Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\\n63: \\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\\n\"}\r\n{\"step_index\":1595,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:58:27Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_branch.lean\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"View test_branch.lean\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View test_branch.lean\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1596,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:58:29Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:58:29+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:58:29+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_branch.lean`\\nTotal Lines: 20\\nTotal Bytes: 674\\nShowing lines 1 to 20\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: import Mathlib\\n2: import LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n3: \\n4: open SimpleGraph\\n5: open GraphCalc\\n6: \\n7: -- Let's test what Lean says about the remaining branch\\n8: theorem test_goal {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n9:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n10:     (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G)\\n11:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadi